C++ code snippet:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> numbers = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
    std::sort(numbers.begin(), numbers.end(), std::greater<int>());
    for (int num : numbers) {
        std::cout << num << " ";
    }
    return 0;
}
```

This code sorts a vector of integers in descending order and prints the sorted numbers. The code is well-structured and follows best practices for C++ programming.
